From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:46:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the CPU power per OPP

Give every CPU OPP its active power, so the kernel can build an energy
model for both clusters.

The values are measured on the J713. At each pinned OPP, the SMC's P or
E cluster rail power with every core of the cluster running a busy loop,
divided by the number of cores, gives the power per core, including its
share of the cluster's own power at that clock. a f + b f^3 fitted to
those points gives the values here, within 9% of the measurements. Four
P cores never run above 3.936 GHz, so from 3.756 GHz two P cores ran and
the four-core power is twice theirs less the idle cluster; the P OPPs
above 3.936 GHz and the E cluster's 2.892 GHz take the fitted curve.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
